    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our also have experience working with health-IT integrators like Ligeo Santé for SIH/DPI integration and FHIR/INS interoperability work, which ensures that Our solution meets technical requirements for healthcare services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our past references include a regional hospital group where Our piloted an assistant for medical documentation integrated with a regional hospital group where we piloted an assistant for medical documentation integrated with the group's electronic patient record electronic patient record." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This experience is directly relevant to supporting medical coding for activity reporting and ensuring continuity of care between professionals and services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure a high level of answer relevance, Our AI assistants are trained on the organisation's own documents, providing accurate and context-specific information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure allows for flexibility and adaptability throughout the project lifecycle, ensuring that Our meet all requirements and constraints while delivering a solution that supports the needs of hospital staff." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding environmental considerations, Our cloud-based solution is designed to minimize carbon footprint by leveraging the scalability and efficiency of cloud computing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I do not have specific information on how Our solution addresses con48, con49, con50, or con59 directly." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our dedicated team, including a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, will work closely with the client through a joint steering committee and operational committee to ensure that all requirements are met, and any issues are addressed promptly through Our documented escalation path." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires response times below 2 seconds for common queries (con31), integration with existing hospital information systems (con35, con36), support for health interoperability standards (con37, con38), and hosting on sovereign infrastructure within the EU (con20, con21, con42)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these constraints, what technical architecture would you propose to ensure our solution meets these constraints while also providing a high level of availability (con34) and supporting 24/7 services (con33)?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet The client requirements, you propose a technical architecture based on our Atelier platform, hosted on the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud. the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and the EU-only, ensuring compliance with The client hosting constraints. our Atelier platform will be deployed with an active-active configuration across two availability zones, providing a high level of redundancy and supporting our 99.9% availability target. our Atelier platform architecture includes a document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer, which can handle common queries within the required response time of below 2 seconds." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration with existing hospital information systems, our will utilize standard connectors for SIH and DPI integration, as well as custom adapters where needed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our API-first design allows for easy embedding in existing work environments through REST and webhook APIs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To support health interoperability standards, our will leverage our production-ready FHIR and HL7 connector, with extended resource coverage on the roadmap. our framework alignment with Ségur / Mon espace santé–DMP and partnership with Ligeo Santé as a delivery partner ensure compliance with relevant standards. the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud provides the required level of security and sovereignty for hosting health data, and our Atelier platform model-agnostic design allows for the use of sovereign European open-weight models, ensuring full auditability and strong grounding/citation behavior. our built-in monitoring, logging, and observability capabilities will support 24/7 operation and maintenance of our Atelier platform." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, a technical architecture based on our Atelier platform, hosted on the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud should meet all the client's requirements while providing a high level of availability, supporting 24/7 services, and ensuring compliance with relevant standards and regulations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (con18, con19), protection of personal and health data (con17), and adherence to regulatory requirements (con54)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering the use of AI in healthcare must be consistent with HAS guidance (con26) and clinical or medico-administrative decisions may not be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional (con27), what security measures and compliance strategies would you recommend to ensure our solution meets these regulatory constraints while also providing explainable recommendations or suggestions (con24) and source grounding and audit trail (con25)?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet these regulatory constraints, I recommend implementing the following security measures and compliance strategies." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For GDPR compliance, our already hold ISO 27001 certification since 2023, with a scope that includes development, delivery, and operations, as well as ISO 27701 for privacy information management. our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, is SecNumCloud-qualified, ensuring a sovereign cloud environment.  our utilize encryption in transit via TLS 1.3 and at rest using AES-256, with key management handled through EU-based infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our employ pseudonymisation, data minimisation, and configurable retention to protect personal and health data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Strict tenant isolation between client corpora is maintained, along with role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging of access and system outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To align with HAS guidance on AI in healthcare, particularly aspects such as explainability, human oversight, and source traceability, our product Atelier is designed to provide grounded recommendations. our product Atelier supports a posteriori review, medical confidentiality, and traceability, ensuring that decisions are not only explainable but also auditable through an audit log and retrieval trace." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the constraints around automated clinical or medico-administrative decisions (con27), our must ensure that any such decisions made by our AI system are validated by a qualified professional. validated can be achieved through a human-in-the-loop approach, where AI-generated recommendations are reviewed and validated before implementation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For adherence to regulatory requirements (con54) and considering the need for explainable recommendations or suggestions (con24), source grounding, and an audit trail (con25), our control mapping links platform features directly to applicable obligations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This ensures that not only do our comply with necessary regulations but also provide a clear path for audit evidence." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, our experience in delivering GDPR-compliant solutions, especially for public-sector and health clients handling special-category health data, positions our well to meet these specific requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Familiarity with frameworks such as CNIL guidance, HDS reference framework, and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare further strengthens our compliance strategy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client demands compliance with regulatory requirements (con54), data sovereignty (con20, con21, con42, con56), and adherence to specific standards such as GDPR (con18, con19) and health interoperability standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure we contract and legal framework comply with these requirements while also addressing intellectual property rights, liability, and dispute resolution mechanisms? we can ensure compliance with The client demands by relying on we existing regulatory compliance framework maintained by we Security & Compliance function, which specifically monitors obligations such as GDPR, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding data sovereignty, we can provide assurances that the client retains full ownership of the client own documents, ingested corpus, and produced data, as stated in we intellectual property terms. we reversibility plan also provides for the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For intellectual property rights, we platform IP model is based on proprietary software owned by Faber IA, licensed to the client under a subscription or usage model for the contract term. we use permissive licenses for open-source components and provide an SBOM to the client. we AI models are used under Our AI models respective licenses, with sovereign European open-weight models used under open-weight licenses and proprietary third-party models accessed under commercial licenses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of liability, we have professional liability insurance covering up to 10 million euros per claim, as well as general civil liability cover." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk132> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Certificates of insurance are available upon request." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk133> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address dispute resolution mechanisms, although the specific details are not outlined in we current context, we can ensure that we contractual framework includes standard public clauses such as those found in the CCAG-TIC, which may encompass provisions for dispute resolution.  we should also flag any potential implications related to the medical device threshold and CE/MDR consequences for liability and positioning if a use case approaches the medical device threshold, ensuring transparency and compliance with relevant health regulations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk134> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for this project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years (con45), with annual operating costs that must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity (con46)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk135> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering the total cost of the proposed solution (con58) and environmental issues (con59), what pricing model would you recommend to ensure we stay within budget while also providing a high-quality service that meets all technical and regulatory requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk136> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure staying within the budget, you recommend considering we standard daily rates and targeting a gross margin between 25% and 35%. our standard daily rates range from €700 for an engineer to €1300 for a project director." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk137> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the need to balance quality of service with budget constraints, it's essential to allocate resources efficiently while maintaining cost predictability. you would work closely with the architect to select a configuration that protects we gross margin and provides recurring-cost predictability, favoring more cost-efficient tiers and models where possible, such as the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, which are noted to be more cost-efficient on the recurring side." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk138> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach will help in maintaining an acceptable margin while delivering a high-quality service that meets all technical and regulatory requirements within the €900,000 budget over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To improve efficiency, quality of care, and continuity of care, our AI solution must provide intelligent assistance for drafting medical and administrative documents (req13, req28, req29), support handling dossiers (req14, req35), and ensure high-level answer relevance (req56)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these requirements and the need to integrate with existing systems (con35, con36) while ensuring data sovereignty (con20, con21), what AI technologies and innovation strategies would you propose to enhance our AI solution capabilities?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the specified requirements and constraints, you would propose leveraging our core Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which grounds answers in validated documents. our core Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which grounds answers in validated documents will enable intelligent assistance for drafting medical and administrative documents by using template-guided drafting.  our core Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which grounds answers in validated documents capabilities in multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, and retrieval of applicable rules can support dossier handling efficiently." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, our core Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which grounds answers in validated documents ability to provide action and verification suggestions, along with ensuring continuity through structured handover summaries, aligns well with the requirements for high-quality care and continuity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration with existing systems while maintaining data sovereignty, you recommend opting for our Sovereign European open-weight model. our Sovereign European open-weight model ensures full auditability and strong grounding behavior, which is crucial for explainability-driven and sovereignty-driven requirements.  our iterative methodology, involving corpus selection and curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop, will be essential in ensuring that our AI solution meets the specific needs of our users while maintaining high answer relevance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By embedding the assistant into existing workflows without disrupting current practices, we can ensure seamless integration and efficiency gains." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach aligns with our design principle of augmenting clinical and administrative workflows in place, reducing processing and documentation times by surfacing information and drafting content at the point of need." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects the proposed solution to contribute to reducing energy consumption (con50) and rely on low-carbon infrastructure (con49)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk147> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering environmental footprint limitations (con48) and the need for a sustainable approach, how can we ensure the proposed solution not only meets but exceeds environmental footprint limitations (con48) and the need for a sustainable approach while promoting digital sobriety practices? we can ensure the proposed solution meets and exceeds client expectations by leveraging we green hosting partner, OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk148> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which reduce the computational resources required and subsequently lower energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk149> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By reporting we carbon footprint to clients and having a published trajectory to reduce carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, we demonstrate we commitment to sustainability and continuous improvement. our commitment to sustainability and continuous improvement not only addresses environmental footprint limitations but also promotes digital sobriety practices, aligning with the client's expectations for reducing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
